      <h2 class="section__title">Common Mistakes Brands Make with Pakistan Manufacturers</h2>
      <p class="section__text">
        Working with Pakistan manufacturers offers significant advantages, but brands make avoidable mistakes that can undermine these benefits. Learn from these common pitfalls to ensure smooth production and maximize Pakistan's textile advantages.
      </p>
      
      <h3 class="section__subtitle">Underestimating Cotton Quality Variations</h3>
      <p class="section__text">
        Pakistan produces various cotton qualities. Some brands assume all Pakistan Cotton is the same quality, leading to disappointment when they receive lower-grade fabric. Specify your cotton requirements: combed vs carded, ringspun vs open-end, staple length. Request fabric samples before bulk production. SDF provides different cotton quality options and educates clients on the differences, ensuring you get the fabric quality matching your brand positioning.
      </p>
      
      <h3 class="section__subtitle">Ignoring Seasonal Cotton Supply</h3>
      <p class="section__text">
        Pakistan has cotton harvest seasons (typically September to December). Fabric prices and availability can fluctuate based on harvest yields. Some brands lock in prices without considering seasonal factors, potentially missing better pricing or facing delays. Plan your production timeline with cotton harvest cycles in mind. SDF advises clients on optimal timing for cotton sourcing and can secure fabric during harvest at favorable rates.
      </p>
      
      <h3 class="section__subtitle">Not Leveraging GSP Plus for EU Markets</h3>
      <p class="section__text">
        Pakistan's GSP Plus status provides duty-free access to EU markets - a significant competitive advantage. Some brands sourcing from Pakistan fail to optimize their supply chain for EU-bound shipments, missing out on this benefit. Structure your Pakistan operations for EU markets to maximize duty savings. SDF has extensive experience shipping to EU countries under GSP Plus and can guide you on documentation and compliance requirements.
      </p>
      
      <h3 class="section__subtitle">Overlooking Denim Expertise</h3>
      <p class="section__text">
        Pakistan is a major denim producer with advanced washing and finishing capabilities. Some brands source denim garments from Pakistan but don't utilize the country's denim expertise, resulting in generic washes. Work with manufacturers who can develop custom denim washes and finishes. SDF's Pakistan partners offer advanced denim capabilities including enzyme washes, stone washes, and sustainable finishing techniques.
      </p>
      
      <h3 class="section__subtitle">Insufficient Tech Pack Detail for Cotton Garments</h3>
      <p class="section__text">
        Cotton garments have specific construction requirements different from synthetic fabrics. Vague tech packs lead to samples that don't leverage Pakistan's cotton advantages. Specify cotton-specific details: fabric weight, shrinkage expectations, pre-shrinking requirements, stitching types suitable for cotton (e.g., coverstitch for stretch cotton). Invest in cotton-focused tech packs to maximize Pakistan's manufacturing strengths.
      </p>
      
      <h3 class="section__subtitle">Not Verifying Organic Certification Chain</h3>
      <p class="section__text">
        Pakistan has GOTS-certified organic cotton production, but the certification chain must be verified from farm to garment. Some brands accept organic claims without verifying transaction certificates. Always request GOTS transaction certificates for organic cotton to ensure chain-of-custody integrity. SDF provides complete documentation for organic materials, supporting your sustainability claims with verifiable proof.
      </p>
    </div>
